{"id": "sim4-d4-D016-0028-1", "decision": "fix_clean", "clean": "Notes from the harbour meeting. The new terminal building is about three weeks behind schedule, the contractor blames the rain. The council wants a decision on the parking charges by the end of the quarter, and the options are a flat fee of £5 or a sliding scale based on hours. I'd go with the flat fee, it's simpler. Dario raised that the gangway on berth two is wearing out and may need replacing before spring, rough cost around 40,000. We also agreed to trial a bicycle storage area near the ticket office. Action points, I chase the contractor, Dario gets a quote on the gangway.", "reason": "added_fact", "note": "currency not spoken for 'forty thousand'; don't add pound sign"}
